      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of women who attended the party. We can use the given information about the number of men and the number of dances they participated in to set up an equation.\n\n1. **Identify the number of dances per man:**\n   Each man danced with exactly 3 women.\n\n2. **Identify the number of dances per woman:**\n   Each woman danced with exactly 2 men.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of dances:**\n   Since there are 12 men and each man danced with 3 women, the total number of dances can be calculated as:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total dances} = 12 \\text{ men} \\times 3 \\text{ women per man} = 36 \\text{ dances}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the number of women:**\n   Each woman danced with 2 men. Therefore, the total number of dances can also be expressed as:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total dances} = 2 \\text{ men per woman} \\times \\text{Number of women}\n   \\]\n   Let \\( w \\) be the number of women. Then:\n   \\[\n   36 = 2w\n   \\]\n\n5. **Solve for \\( w \\):**\n   \\[\n   w = \\frac{36}{2} = 18\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of women who attended the party is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
